age when linked. So there you go. As I said before, enjoy digging through 700 pages. Perhaps if you did your research based on actual court dockets and responses instead of putting blind faith in any media source...<br /> <br /> EDIT: Whoops, sorry, that's the probate/family/land court. The general one is <a href=\"http://www.ma-appellatecourts.org/search.php\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.ma-appellatecourts.org/search.php</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2058,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2058-nobody","user":"Nobody","date":". 06-28-2014, 07:12 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2058-nobody","name":"Nobody","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-28T05:27:18-07:00","id":182817,"title":"","content":"<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blue Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/181472-massachusetts-swat-teams-claim-they\u2019re-private-corporations?p=182704#post182704\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Shadowflame, I'm sure Nobody doesn't have his cow at the ditch here and neither do we, which doesn't mean that quotes or links wouldn't be nice if his already found the relevant right information on the topic.</div> </div> </div> </div>*shrugs* Relevant information is great...but not showing where it's sourced? After all if its from some corporate-libertarian website then it's probable not very reliable. <br /> Either the ACLU is being frivolous and hasn't a point in their respective lawsuits or there is merit and concern about hiding info to protect against liability which should not only be investigated but pursued at all levels. Militarization of the police force is a &quot;thing&quot; now. Is there any denial here on that?<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://time.com/2916554/aclu-police-militarized-report-swat-war-comes-home/\" target=\"_blank\">SWAT Teams Treat U.S. Neighborhoods \u2018Like a War Zone\u2019</a><br /> <i><br /> \u202250% people impacted by SWAT deployments from 2011 to 2012 are black or Latino. Whites account for 20%.<br /> \u2022Seven civilians were killed and 46 injured in such deployments from 2010 to 2013.<br /> \u202279% of all SWAT deployments were to execute search warrants for homes, most of them for drug searches.<br /> \u20227% of deployments were for hostage, barricade or active-shooter scenarios.<br /> <br /> Tragic case studies accompany the figures, among them that of Tarika Wilson, a 26-year-old mother who was shot and killed holding her 14-month-old son, and Eurie Stamp, a 68-year-old grandfather who was shot while watching baseball in his pajamas during a SWAT invasion. Bounkham Phonesavanh, a 19-month-old baby, was in a medically induced coma after paramilitary squads unwittingly threw a flash grenade into his crib, piercing a hole in his cheek, chest and scarring his body with third-degree burns. None of the victims were suspects.<br /> <br /> The ACLU claims the militarization of policing in the U.S. lacks oversight and transparency. Not a single law-enforcement agency provided documents of all information \u201cnecessary to undertake a thorough examination of police militarization.\u201d</i><br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-28T06:01:19-07:00","id":182824,"title":"","content":"I gave you the source, but you didn't look it up. Learn how to do your own research rather than just blindly trusting what a media outlet which has its own bias as much as some corporate-libertarian website does.<br /> <br /> In a nutshell: don't trust any bias, especially your own.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2058-nobody","name":"Nobody","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-28T11:23:17-07:00","id":183098,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowflame</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/181472-massachusetts-swat-teams-claim-they\u2019re-private-corporations?p=182817#post182817\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">*shrugs* Relevant information is great...but not showing where it's sourced? After all if its from some corporate-libertarian website then it's probable not very reliable.<br /> Either the ACLU is being frivolous and hasn't a point in their respective lawsuits or there is merit and concern about hiding info to protect against liability which should not only be investigated but pursued at all levels. Militarization of the police force is a &quot;thing&quot; now. Is there any denial here on that?</div> </div> </div> </div>Eh, there's no argument about the fact that they are not disclosing information, only about how relevant that information is to policing. The discussion about the future is summarized as &quot;well will this encourage refusal to disclose MORE data?&quot; and &quot;Does this represent a risky power balance situation?&quot;<br /> <br /> I'm also having trouble parsing your comment about relevant information sourcing... are you saying that several hundred pages of raw court documentation is a corporate-libertarian bias?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowflame</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/181472-massachusetts-swat-teams-claim-they\u2019re-private-corporations?p=182817#post182817\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"http://time.com/2916554/aclu-police-militarized-report-swat-war-comes-home/\" target=\"_blank\">SWAT Teams Treat U.S. Neighborhoods \u2018Like a War Zone\u2019</a></div> </div> </div> </div>This is a topic flip. Or if you want to get into debate terms, you are offering up the strawman of excessive SWAT deployments and violence as an argument against legal reporting requirements.<br /> <br /> None here have voiced the opinion that SWAT teams are not in need of serious re-evaluation of the uses to which they are applied, in fact it's been something that Nobody has mentioned needs to be looked at seriously at least once if not several times.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowflame</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/181472-massachusetts-swat-teams-claim-they\u2019re-private-corporations?p=182817#post182817\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u202250% people impacted by SWAT deployments from 2011 to 2012 are black or Latino. Whites account for 20%.</div> </div> </div> </div>Kinda a pointless attempt to imply racism in the SWAT deployments. The claim might as well be made that since SWAT teams are deployed against men an order of magnitude more than women they're also insanely sexist. SWAT teams are deployed against street drug dealers, shippers and producers. Hardly surprising the majority of people that get involved with street drugs as consumers or dealers are going to be from the poorest neighborhoods which the census survey says.... are predominantly black or Latino.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowflame</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/181472-massachusetts-swat-teams-claim-they\u2019re-private-corporations?p=182817#post182817\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u2022Seven civilians were killed and 46 injured in such deployments from 2010 to 2013.<br /> \u202279% of all SWAT deployments were to execute search warrants for homes, most of them for drug searches.<br /> \u20227% of deployments were for hostage, barricade or active-shooter scenarios.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh hey 79% against drug related crimes. Shocking. And you can be fairly certain they're not deploying SWAT against a doctor that writes out prescriptions for rich people to abuse, because that can be handled with couple officers followed by a lot of lawyers. SWAT is called in when they think there might be a chance of multiple people, or people with guns.<br /> <br /> And honestly I think that civilian death rate sounds abnormally low. 7 deaths in 3 years?<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowflame</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/181472-massachusetts-swat-teams-claim-they\u2019re-private-corporations?p=182817#post182817\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Tragic case studies accompany the figures, among them that of Tarika Wilson, a 26-year-old mother who was shot and killed holding her 14-month-old son, and Eurie Stamp, a 68-year-old grandfather who was shot while watching baseball in his pajamas during a SWAT invasion. Bounkham Phonesavanh, a 19-month-old baby, was in a medically induced coma after paramilitary squads unwittingly threw a flash grenade into his crib, piercing a hole in his cheek, chest and scarring his body with third-degree burns. None of the victims were suspects.<br /> <br /> The ACLU claims the militarization of policing in the U.S. lacks oversight and transparency. Not a single law-enforcement agency provided documents of all information \u201cnecessary to undertake a thorough examination of police militarization.\u201d[/I]</div> </div> </div> </div>All terrible incidents and reasons to investigate the roll of SWAT in society, I fully agree.<br /> <br /> As a side note, Bounkham Phonesavanh isn't in a coma, he's awake and still healing up nicely in the hospital. There's a chance there's some brain damage though,","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Odd_Canuck is not a topical medication or food product and is not to be taken internally or seriously.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/31-odd_canuck","name":"Odd_Canuck","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar31_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1474"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}